---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const post = {
  title: 'How Quick Replies Can Boost Your Team\'s Productivity',
  date: 'December 20, 2025',
  readTime: '4 min read',
  category: 'Tips & Tricks',
  author: 'WATeamInbox Team'
};
---

<Layout title={`${post.title} - WATeamInbox Blog`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-cyan-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-cyan-800">
          {post.category}
        </span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">{post.readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl" data-testid="blog-post-title">
        {post.title}
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-gray-600">
        <span>By {post.author}</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <time>{post.date}</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Featured Image -->
    <div class="mt-12 flex h-64 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-600 to-cyan-800 md:h-96">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-32 w-32 text-white/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-testid="blog-post-content">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600">
        Quick replies are pre-written message templates that save time and ensure consistent communication. Learn how to set them up and use them effectively.
      </p>

      <h2>What Are Quick Replies?</h2>
      <p>
        Quick replies are reusable message templates that you can insert into conversations with a simple shortcut. Instead of typing the same response repeatedly, you can use a quick reply to instantly populate your message.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-cyan-50 border border-cyan-200 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 text-cyan-600 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
          </svg>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-cyan-800">Time Savings</h4>
            <p class="mt-1 text-cyan-700">Teams report saving 2-3 hours per week using quick replies for common responses.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Creating Effective Quick Replies</h2>

      <h3>The Anatomy of a Good Quick Reply</h3>
      <p>
        Each quick reply has three components:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Shortcut:</strong> A memorable trigger (e.g., <code>/greeting</code>, <code>/hours</code>)</li>
        <li><strong>Title:</strong> A descriptive name for organization</li>
        <li><strong>Content:</strong> The actual message text</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Shortcut Naming Best Practices</h3>
      <p>
        Choose shortcuts that are easy to remember and type:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use lowercase letters</li>
        <li>Keep them short (1-3 words)</li>
        <li>Use descriptive names (<code>/shipping</code> not <code>/s1</code>)</li>
        <li>Use underscores or hyphens for multi-word shortcuts (<code>/order_status</code>)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Quick Reply Examples</h2>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Customer Service Templates</h4>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="rounded bg-cyan-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-sm text-cyan-700">/greeting</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Greeting</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Hello! Thank you for contacting [Company Name]. How can I help you today?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="rounded bg-cyan-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-sm text-cyan-700">/thanks</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Thank You</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Thank you for choosing [Company Name]! If you have any other questions, don't hesitate to ask. Have a great day!</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="rounded bg-cyan-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-sm text-cyan-700">/hold</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Please Hold</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Thank you for your patience. I'm looking into this for you and will get back to you shortly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">E-Commerce Templates</h4>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="rounded bg-cyan-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-sm text-cyan-700">/shipping</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Shipping Info</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">We offer free shipping on orders over $50. Standard delivery takes 3-5 business days, and express shipping takes 1-2 business days.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="rounded bg-cyan-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-sm text-cyan-700">/return</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Return Policy</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">We accept returns within 30 days of purchase. Items must be unused and in original packaging. To start a return, please provide your order number.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="rounded bg-cyan-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-sm text-cyan-700">/track</code>
              <span class="text-sm text-gray-500">Order Tracking</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">To track your order, please provide your order number and I'll look up the shipping status for you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Managing Quick Replies</h2>

      <h3>Accessing Quick Replies</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Navigate to <strong>Settings</strong></li>
        <li>Find the <strong>Quick Replies</strong> section</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Add New</strong> to create a template</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Organizing Your Templates</h3>
      <p>
        As your quick reply library grows, organization becomes important:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use consistent naming conventions</li>
        <li>Group related shortcuts with prefixes (<code>/ship_</code>, <code>/order_</code>)</li>
        <li>Review and update templates regularly</li>
        <li>Remove outdated or unused templates</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Tips for Maximum Productivity</h2>

      <h3>Personalize When Needed</h3>
      <p>
        Quick replies are starting points, not final messages. After inserting a template, personalize it with:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Customer's name</li>
        <li>Specific details about their inquiry</li>
        <li>Relevant order numbers or dates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Train Your Team</h3>
      <p>
        Ensure everyone knows how to use quick replies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Share the shortcuts list with new team members</li>
        <li>Create a quick reference card</li>
        <li>Encourage team members to suggest new templates</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Review and Improve</h3>
      <p>
        Regularly review your quick replies to ensure they're still effective:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Update outdated information (prices, policies, hours)</li>
        <li>Refine wording based on customer feedback</li>
        <li>Add new templates for common questions</li>
        <li>Remove templates that are rarely used</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Quick Replies vs. Automation</h2>
      <p>
        Quick replies are different from automated responses:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Quick Replies</th>
              <th>Automation</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Manually triggered</td>
              <td>Automatically triggered</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Can be personalized before sending</td>
              <td>Sent as-is</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Human in the loop</td>
              <td>No human intervention</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Flexible timing</td>
              <td>Immediate response</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        Quick replies are a simple but powerful tool for improving team productivity. By creating a well-organized library of templates, you can respond faster, maintain consistency, and focus your energy on the conversations that truly need personalized attention.
      </p>

      <p>
        Start with 5-10 templates for your most common responses, then expand as you identify new opportunities for time savings.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Author Bio -->
    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-cyan-100">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-cyan-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{post.author}</p>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Building the future of business communication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back to Blog -->
    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
